<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak harvest estimate 19.1 pct up at 3.12 mln T.</title>
<headline>Slovak harvest estimate 19.1 pct up at 3.12 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovakia's 1997 grain harvest is estimated to yield up to 3.12 million tonnes, an increase of 19.1 percent over 1996, the Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The rapeseed harvest is estimated at between 199,000 and 208,000 tonnes, an increase of 42.6 percent over 1996, SUSR said.</p>
<p>The increases are a result of larger sown areas and bigger estimated yields per hectare, SUSR said.</p>
<p>The grain estimate does not include seed maize, SUSR said.</p>
<p>--Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521 8402</p>
